# Cornell Box -- Wavefront OBJ
# 
# Axis convention: x right, y up, z toward the viewer (right-handed).
# The box occupies [0,1]^3. The camera is placed at z < 0 looking toward +z.
# All face windings are counter-clockwise when viewed from the surface normal side.
# 
# Contents:
#   - Room walls (floor, ceiling, back, left/red, right/green)
#   - Ceiling area light
#   - White cube (box interior, left side)
#   - Blue sphere (box interior, right side)
# 
# Note: the form-factor kernel assumes unit inter-patch visibility.
# The cube and sphere produce no occlusion shadows in this implementation.
# See README.md for the visibility extension roadmap.
# 
# Reference geometry: Goral et al. (1984). ACM SIGGRAPH 84.

mtllib cornell_box.mtl

# --- Room vertices ---

# Floor corners (y = 0)
v 0.0 0.0 0.0
v 1.0 0.0 0.0
v 1.0 0.0 1.0
v 0.0 0.0 1.0

# Ceiling corners (y = 1)
v 0.0 1.0 0.0
v 1.0 1.0 0.0
v 1.0 1.0 1.0
v 0.0 1.0 1.0

# Light patch corners (y = 1, centred: x in [0.43, 0.57], z in [0.43, 0.57])
# Reduced to 0.14 x 0.14 m for a focused spotlight beam.
v 0.43 1.0 0.43
v 0.57 1.0 0.43
v 0.57 1.0 0.57
v 0.43 1.0 0.57

